<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Personalization</h2>
<p>Before launching personalization automation, prove every app in the stack logs email and SMS consent auditably, with purchase events cutting promotional follow-up the moment checkout completes. Personalization audiences forgive plain creative; they do not forgive promos sent mid-refund or right after checkout.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Hold all personalization marketing; transactional only</td><td>Personalization consent is the legal basis of every send</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Personalization education and proof before any offer</td><td>First-touch personalization codes create discount dependence</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Personalization reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Margin-safe personalization recovery at peak intent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Suppress personalization selling after checkout; educate instead</td><td>Spares personalization buyers remorse and unsubscribes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Personalization selling waits for case resolution</td><td>Service-active personalization shoppers reject promos</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Prune unengaged personalization profiles early</td><td>Personalization deliverability depends on pruning</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Personalization texting respects time and frequency rules</td><td>One personalization SMS complaint outweighs many email ones</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Send personalization B2B accounts down their own track</td><td>Personalization retail promos can violate B2B terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Personalization automation skips unverified domains first</td><td>Personalization bounces from junk signups hurt inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Personalization internal accounts never enter production</td><td>Internal personalization activity corrupts program metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Personalization researcher signups follow standard consent</td><td>Manual personalization exceptions rot the audit trail</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Re-permission legacy personalization lists pre-automation</td><td>Personalization compliance demands re-permission</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Personalization</h2>
<p>Attributed revenue is not profit for personalization. A self-funding personalization program survives a full cost model: subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, capture tooling, templates, agency time, and every point of personalization discount margin. For personalization, a stack at fifteen percent of attributed margin needs simplification first, optimization second.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. For personalization, free plans always bind somewhere; identify whether contacts, sends, branching, or support caps your personalization motion first.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Cost component</th><th>What to model</th><th>Common failure</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Platform subscription</td><td>Personalization tier priced at realistic contact scale</td><td>Personalization tier bought for phantom growth</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contact or send overages</td><td>Personalization growth pace versus plan ceilings</td><td>Personalization overage invoices after drops</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS credits</td><td>Personalization opt-in share times texts per journey</td><td>Personalization SMS assumed as cheap email</td></tr>
<tr><td>Discount budget</td><td>Personalization code depth times likely redemption</td><td>personalization flows teaching shoppers to hold out</td></tr>
<tr><td>Creative and ops time</td><td>Personalization upkeep hours per operating week</td><td>personalization maintenance hours wished away</td></tr>
<tr><td>Migration and setup</td><td>personalization switch priced in imports and rebuild labor</td><td>Personalization audit trail gaps after moves</td></tr>
<tr><td>Support and success tiers</td><td>Personalization support tier for critical incidents</td><td>Peak-week personalization outage without coverage</td></tr>
<tr><td>Third-party integrations</td><td>personalization companion tools and their fees</td><td>personalization side-tools eclipsing core cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deliverability remediation</td><td>personalization inbox-health monitoring and cleanup</td><td>personalization sender damage costing more than tools</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
